  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts most people are referring to are most commonly called the **\"Terminal Tackle\"** shirts (long-sleeve tee style). Here's a breakdown of the most popular thin/lightweight PFG options:\n\n1. **Terminal Tackle** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. Equipped with Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, this fishing shirt dries quickly and manages moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n2. **PFG Bahama** \u2013 Featuring angler-friendly details and lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun so you can stay out there longer.\n\n3. **Tamiami** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric, UPF 50 sun protection, hidden mesh-lined vents in the back, and an antimicrobial treatment that helps reduce odor.\n\n4. **Tidal Deflector / Terminal Deflector** \u2013 If you get hot and sweaty when you're on the water, this is one of the best fishing shirts for cooling. Made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology, it uses touch-activated cooling fabric to prevent you from overheating.\n\nThe **Terminal Tackle** and **Bahama** are probably the most iconic \"thin\" PFG shirts that people recognize. The PFG line, which stands for Performance Fishing Gear, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style.",
